{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocket_directive", "label": "websocket() route directive", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Produces a Route, so it composes with path(), concat() and withMiddleware() like any other part of the DSL."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketserveractor", "label": "WebsocketServerActor (the hub)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One actor per route sees every connection event serialized, so the actor-model guarantee applies \u2014 no concurrent handler execution, no locks. Type parameters read from the server point of view: TOut is what the server sends, TIn what it receives."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketconnection", "label": "WebsocketConnection<TOut>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It extends ActorRef but cannot be deathwatched \u2014 onClientDisconnected is the single, ordered end-of-life signal per connection."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketrouteoptions", "label": "WebsocketRouteOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Precedence is route options > HOCON (actor-ts.http.websocket) > built-in defaults."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxframebytes", "label": "maxFrameBytes checked at two moments", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The transport cap refuses an oversize frame while it arrives (client sees 1006, since the runtime hangs up rather than sending a policy close); the connection actor checks the fully received frame before decode and closes with 1009. Only the second is a guarantee \u2014 the transport cap is an optimisation that spares the process the buffering. Resolution happens at bind(), so a malformed value fails there rather than on the first upgrade."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_transport_cap_gaps", "label": "Two runtime/backend pairs have no transport cap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deno upgradeWebSocket exposes no payload limit at all; and on Bun with Express or Fastify the ws specifier resolves to Bun built-in shim, which accepts maxPayload and reads it back unchanged while enforcing nothing \u2014 measured, a 2 MiB frame against a 1 MiB cap reached the handler intact where Node refused it at the socket. The guarantee holds but the memory is spent before the refusal, so front an internet-facing endpoint with a proxy."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_shared_transport_widest_cap", "label": "A shared transport takes the widest cap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A server has one transport shared by all its WebSocket routes, so where routes disagree the stricter one still refuses its oversize frames with 1009 \u2014 it just loses the narrower buffering window."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_allowedorigins", "label": "allowedOrigins (CSWSH defence)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Browsers attach cookies to a WS upgrade automatically, so any page can ride the victim credentials on an ambiently-authenticated route. A listed-but-unmatched Origin is rejected with 403 before the handshake; a missing Origin is allowed because CSWSH is browser-only. Matters most for cookie- or IP-based auth, since browsers cannot set Authorization on a handshake."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxconnections", "label": "maxConnections", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxbufferedbytes", "label": "maxBufferedBytes / onBackpressure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When a client cannot keep up its send buffer grows; past the bound the connection drops frames or is closed. Broadcasts to many slow clients are where this bites."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_jsoncodec", "label": "jsonCodec()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_rawcodec", "label": "rawCodec()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketcodec", "label": "WebsocketCodec<TOut, TIn>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketdecodeerror", "label": "WebsocketDecodeError / onInvalidMessage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Policy is close (1003), drop, or hook \u2014 the hook routes decode failures to the actor onInvalidMessage instead of closing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_per_connection_ordering", "label": "Per-connection ordering", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "onClientConnected once, then zero or more onMessage in frame order, then exactly one onClientDisconnected."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_connection_actor", "label": "Internal connection actor (child of the hub)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "onReceive is sealed on a WebsocketServerActor: the framework spawns a child per connection that owns the socket, decodes inbound frames, writes outbound and is stopped when the socket closes. You implement onMessage and the hooks instead."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_hub_mailbox_bounding", "label": "Bounding the hub mailbox", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The command that spawns a connection actor travels the same exempt lane a death-watch Terminated takes: it is sent exactly once from the upgrade callback and carries the only reference to a socket whose handshake completed \u2014 losing it would leave that socket upgraded with nothing attached, frames piling up unread and its maxConnections slot held. What a bound does shed is inbound frames and the connected/disconnected signals, so a bounded hub can hand you a client that never appears in this.clients or never leaves it. Prefer maxConnections and maxFrameBytes, which bound the input rather than the accepted backlog."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_middleware_at_upgrade", "label": "Middleware runs at upgrade time", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "withMiddleware runs once against the HTTP upgrade request, not per message, so auth middleware gates the handshake. Backend-native middleware runs too \u2014 Fastify route hooks, Express and Hono app.use \u2014 and the framework own guard runs after all of them, so withMiddleware and allowedOrigins always have the last word."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketupgradeinfo", "label": "WebsocketUpgradeInfo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_hono_node_ws_version_gate", "label": "Hono on Node needs @hono/node-ws 1.2.0+", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The cap is written onto the ws server handed back as wss, a member that only exists from 1.2.0; rather than bind an uncapped socket the backend refuses to build the WebSocket bridge and names the version in the error."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocket_directive", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketserveractor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocket_directive", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketrouteoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocket_directive", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_route_dsl", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketrouteoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxframebytes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketrouteoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxconnections", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketrouteoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxbufferedbytes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketrouteoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_allowedorigins", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxframebytes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_transport_cap_gaps", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxframebytes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_shared_transport_widest_cap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxframebytes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_hono_node_ws_version_gate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_maxframebytes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_connection_actor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketserveractor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketconnection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/websocket.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_websocketserveractor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_websocket_per_connection_ordering", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", 